Also, developBugAndCreatePR delegates and returns `result` — if developTicket throws (prCreationFailure/gitOperationsFailure), the outer catch of developBugAndCreatePR catches it and returns `{success:false, error}` — hmm! That would swallow the marked error and convert to a return value... wait no: the outer catch in developBugAndCreatePR catches the throw from developTicket.action and returns success:false. That breaks the "fail the run loudly" contract for the bug flow!

Look at developBugAndCreatePR catch:
```js
} catch (error) {
    console.error('❌ Error in developBugAndCreatePR:', error);
    ...
    return { success: false, error: error.toString() };
}
