### 1b. Loud PR-creation failure (missing-PR must not read as plain success)

Following gh-683 pattern. Add:

```js
/**
 * Throws a marked Error so a Pull-Request-Creation failure propagates out of
 * action() and the workflow run is RED (same mechanism and rationale as
 * throwGitOperationsFailure — gh-683). Live fa gh-1197 (run 37234028759,
 * 2026-10-04): the dev leg's PR-creation tail died silently, NO PR existed,
 * and the leg still reported success and armed review. resetDevelopmentForRetry()
 * has ALREADY posted the stage comment and reset the ticket before this throws.
 */
function throwPrCreationFailure(stage, errorMessage) {
    var err = new Error('Pull Request creation failure (' + stage + '): ' + errorMessage);
    err.prCreationFailure = true;
    throw err;
}
```

And in the `!prResult.success` block:
```js
if (!prResult.success) {
    console.error('❌ Pull Request creation failed:', prResult.error);
    if (resumeDevelopmentAgent(...)) return action(params);
    resetDevelopmentForRetry(...);
    // gh-729: ticket is reset for retry — fail the RUN so a no-PR leg is a
    // visible dead letter instead of a green silent success.
    throwPrCreationFailure('Pull Request Creation', prResult.error);
}
```
And in the outer catch: `if (error && error.prCreationFailure) throw error;`

